    "created_at": "2020-01-03T14:49:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-03T14:49:24Z",
    "body": "Ideally I'd prefer it was inherited from its immediate parent like the about:blank iframe's origin.  I don't know if that is reasonable for COOP, though.  If the parent's COOP policy was inherited from its parent and so on, it would kind of devolve to inheriting from the top-level, but a frame in the middle could change the policy with a header?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
